  "subtitle": "every Sofia's planet",
  "story": "On Sofia, armchairs inch towards whoever their owner loves, about a foot a year. Newlyweds' chairs start at opposite ends of the lounge, and you can tell how long a couple's been married with a tape measure. Brenda and Ken's chairs started either side of the fireplace. Every year they shuffled a little closer, mostly while they were asleep in them. By their silver wedding, they touched, right in front of the screen. Nobody can get to the telly.",
