    "end": "Nobody can get to the telly.",
    "caption": "Neither armchair is where it started.\n\nSofia: 1.7 million people, a 26-hour day, no moons, and armchairs that inch towards whoever their owner loves, about a foot a year. Newlyweds' chairs start at opposite ends of the lounge, and you can tell how long a couple's been married with a tape measure. Brenda and Ken's started either side of the fireplace, a very long time ago.\n\nI stayed a week in a hotel there. By the last night, my armchair was up against the minibar.\n\n(The story goes that the Victorians made an S-shaped 'courting chair', so a couple could sit face to face without quite touching. On Sofia, give it a silver wedding.)\n\nWhich of you would do most of the inching?"
  },
